SOAPBOX: Something told me to expedite getting my mast up. My fiberglass
SOAPBOX: mask was taken down by a microburst last summer and I just got it
SOAPBOX: back up in the air a couple of days before this contest began. I
SOAPBOX: didn't get in until Saturday night. And boy, were the bands quiet
SOAPBOX: as far as noise.. The signal to noise ratio was superb about an
SOAPBOX: S3. Even without the filters on. A lot of activity, so I jumped
SOAPBOX: in S and P. And seemed to do pretty good for the most part, Not
SOAPBOX: bad for an inverted sloper 160 that I bought a few years ago.
SOAPBOX: Looking forward to the next one next year...
